  grid: 4-13 rows x 10-15 cols, bg=0
  palette:
    shape: 2xN or Nx2 block on one grid edge (top/bottom/left/right)
    entries: 2-5 pairs; outer row/col = border-key colors (all distinct, all non-bg), inner row/col = fill colors (all distinct)
    no bg cells within palette region
    isolated from all sprites (no 4-adjacent non-bg cell outside palette shares its color)
  sprites:
    count: 2-4 distinct single-color hollow shapes on bg, each separated from others and palette by >=1 bg cell
    each sprite is a connected or near-connected region of one non-bg color forming a closed or semi-closed boundary with >=1 enclosed bg hole
    bbox: 3-7 rows x 3-6 cols, cell count 8-16
    filled_sprites: 1-3 sprites whose border color appears as a palette key; their enclosed holes get filled with the mapped fill color
    distractor_sprite: exactly 1 sprite whose border color is NOT a palette key; its holes stay unfilled
    palette may also contain extra entries (border keys with no corresponding sprite): 1-3 unused entries [observed]
  transformation:
    for each enclosed bg region not touching grid boundary, find dominant adjacent border color; if in palette mapping, fill hole with mapped fill color; otherwise leave unchanged
    palette block itself is unchanged

generation_strategy:
  approach: output-first
  steps:
    1. Pick grid size (4-13 x 10-15), bg=0, palette side (top/bottom/left/right), and palette length N (2-5).
    2. Choose 2N+1 to 2N+3 distinct non-bg colors; assign N as border-keys, N as fill-values, remainder for sprites not in palette.
    3. Build palette 2xN block: outer line = border-key colors, inner line = fill colors. Place on chosen edge.
    4. Generate 2-4 hollow single-color sprites (bbox 3-7 x 3-6) with 1-2 enclosed holes each. For filled sprites, use a palette border-key color and pre-fill holes with the mapped fill color (output state). For the 1 distractor sprite, use a color NOT in palette keys and leave holes as bg.
    5. Place sprites on grid separated from each other and palette by >=1 bg cell.
    6. Save grid as output. To get input, replace all filled-hole cells back to bg.
